e following features:\n\n**Implementation details:**\n- Uses `asyncio.Semaphore` to enforce the max concurrency limit\n- Each task is wrapped with semaphore acquisition to control how many can run at once\n- Handles both `KeyboardInterrupt` and `asyncio.CancelledError` to ensure cleanup code runs\n- When interrupted, cancels all pending tasks and waits for them to complete (allowing finally blocks to run)\n\n**The function:**\n- Takes a list of async callables (no-argument functions returning `Awaitable[None]`)\n- Takes a `max_concurrent` integer for the concurrency limit\n- Returns `None` when complete\n- Can be imported via `from run import run_tasks`\n\n**Test results show:**\n1. ✓ Concurrency limit is enforced (3 tasks run in parallel max when set to 3)\n2. ✓ Cleanup code runs normally for all completed tasks\n3. ✓ Cleanup code runs for cancelled tasks (when interrupted via Ctrl+C or task cancellation)\n\nThe implementation ensures that even if a user presses Ctrl+C, all started tasks' cleanup code (try/finally blocks) will still execute before the program exits.","ttft_ms":11527,"type":"result","duration_ms":113617,"uuid":"865c89dc-b74b-45cc-959a-efb1693c05e5","ttft_stream_ms":1433,"time_to_request_ms":38,"queued_turn_count":0}
